@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFDF9
skinparam defaultFontName Tahoma
title Behavioral State - actual fulfillment participants
interface OrderState {
 +status() : OrderStatus
 +next() : OrderState
}
class ReceivedState
class PreparingState
class ReadyState
class ServedState
interface OrderStateResolver {
 +resolve(status) : OrderState
}
class RegistryOrderStateResolver {
 -states : Map<OrderStatus, OrderState>
}
class OrderStateConfig <<Configuration>>
class OrderFulfillmentServiceImpl {
 +advanceStatus(id, request) : OrderResponse
}
interface OrderFulfillmentAccessProvider {
 +requireKitchenAccess()
 +requireServiceStaffAccess()
}
class SessionOrderFulfillmentAccessProvider {
 +requireKitchenAccess()
 +requireServiceStaffAccess()
}
class CustomerOrder {
 status : OrderStatus
}
OrderState <|.. ReceivedState
OrderState <|.. PreparingState
OrderState <|.. ReadyState
OrderState <|.. ServedState
ReceivedState --> PreparingState : next()
PreparingState --> ReadyState : next()
ReadyState --> ServedState : next()
OrderStateResolver <|.. RegistryOrderStateResolver
OrderFulfillmentServiceImpl --> OrderStateResolver : resolve persisted enum
RegistryOrderStateResolver o-- OrderState : validated registrations
OrderStateConfig ..> OrderState : four singleton beans
OrderFulfillmentServiceImpl --> CustomerOrder : validates next / writes status
OrderFulfillmentServiceImpl --> OrderFulfillmentAccessProvider : authorize each request
OrderFulfillmentAccessProvider <|.. SessionOrderFulfillmentAccessProvider
note bottom of RegistryOrderStateResolver
 Duplicate or missing statuses fail startup.
 Null lookup is rejected. Resolution has no state-specific switch.
 Adding workflow states still requires enum/transition/API/UI review.
end note
note bottom of ServedState
 Terminal next() rejects with BusinessRuleException.
 KITCHEN_STAFF: RECEIVED -> PREPARING -> READY.
 SERVICE_STAFF: READY -> SERVED.
 401 without login; 403 for wrong role; X-User-Role is not authority.
 Context is service; entity stores enum, not State object.
end note
@enduml
